/* 

  Probability of winning an election - Trump vs Harris in Picat.

  What is the probability of Trump or Harris (or other) winning given forecasts,
  i.e. that they get more votes than the two other?

  From Nate Silver
  (as of writing 2024-11-03 @09:34, CEST)
  https://www.natesilver.net/p/nate-silver-2024-president-election-polls-model

  Probability of national winning;
  - Trump: 0.476
  - Harris: 0.485
  

  Cf
  - ppl_voting_probabilities.pi 
  - my Gamble model gamble_voting_trump_harris.rkt

  This program was created by Hakan Kjellerstrand, hakank@gmail.com
  See also my Picat page: http://www.hakank.org/picat/

*/

import ppl_distributions, ppl_utils.
import util.
% import ordset.

main => go.

/*

  As can be noted, as the votes increases, the probability of Trump
  winning decreases.

[trump_prob = 0.476,harris_prob = 0.485,num_votes = 10]
